                                <textField key="contentView" focusRingType="none" verticalHuggingPriority="750" horizontalCompressionResistancePriority="250" textFieldBorderShape="none" translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints="NO" id="pgl-FF-UYx">
                                    <rect key="frame" x="104" y="144" width="397" height="210"/>
                                    <textFieldCell key="cell" selectable="YES" enabled="NO" id="yTx-z3-hXK">
                                        <font key="font" textStyle="footnote" name=".SFNS-Regular"/>
                                        <string key="title">This setting determines how creation and modification timestamps are corrected according to the discrepancy between the local time and the AFP server's time.

"Correct any clock difference" will always convert the server's file timestamps relative to the difference between server and local time.

"Correct time zone differences only" will convert the server's file timestamps relative to the difference between server and local time only if the server time is within 14 hours of the local time (indicating that the server's time is likely set correctly but in a different time zone than the local host).

"Assume the server is in this Mac's local time zone" will ignore the server's clock entirely, and interpret all file timestamps as if they were local timestamps in this Mac's time zone.</string>
                                        <color key="textColor" name="secondaryLabelColor" catalog="System" colorSpace="catalog"/>
                                        <color key="backgroundColor" name="textBackgroundColor" catalog="System" colorSpace="catalog"/>
                                    </textFieldCell>
                                </textField>
